(window.IND_GITA_V = window.IND_GITA_V || {})[17] = [{"v":1,"sp":"arjuna","spm":null,"spl":"अर्जुन उवाच","spp":"before","sa":"ये शास्त्रविधिमुत्सृज्य यजन्ते श्रद्धयाऽन्विताः ।\nतेषां निष्ठा तु का कृष्ण सत्त्वमाहो रजस्तमः ॥","iast":"ye śāstravidhimutsṛjya yajante śraddhayā’nvitāḥ |\nteṣāṃ niṣṭhā tu kā kṛṣṇa sattvamāho rajastamaḥ ||","read":"ye shaastravidhimutsrijya yajante shraddhayaa'nvitaah |\nteshaam nishthaa tu kaa krishna sattvamaaho rajastamah ||","spli":"arjuna uvāca","splr":"arjuna uvaacha","en":"Arjuna said: Those that sacrifice full of faith, but casting aside the ordinances of the Scriptures, what is verily their condition, O Krishna? Is it one of Purity, Passion, or Darkness?","en2":"Those who setting aside the ordinance of the Shâstra, perform sacrifice with Shraddhâ, what is their condition, O Krishna? (Is it) Sattva, Rajas or Tamas?","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":2,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":"श्री भगवानुवाच","spp":"before","sa":"त्रिविधा भवति श्रद्धा देहिनां सा स्वभावजा ।\nसात्त्विकी राजसी चैव तामसी चेति तां शृणु ॥","iast":"trividhā bhavati śraddhā dehināṃ sā svabhāvajā |\nsāttvikī rājasī caiva tāmasī ceti tāṃ śṛṇu ||","read":"trividhaa bhavati shraddhaa dehinaam saa svabhaavajaa |\nsaattvikee raajasee chaiva taamasee cheti taam shrinu ||","spli":"śrī bhagavānuvāca","splr":"shree bhagavaanuvaacha","en":"The Blessed Lord said: Threefold is by nature the inborn faith of the embodied—pure, passionate, and dark. Hear thou of these.","en2":"Threefold is the Shraddhâ of the embodied, which is inherent in their nature,—the Sâttvika, the Râjasika and the Tâmasika. Do thou hear of it.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":3,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सत्त्वानुरूपा सर्वस्य श्रद्धा भवति भारत ।\nश्रद्धामयोऽयं पुरुषो यो यच्छ्रद्धः स एव सः ॥","iast":"sattvānurūpā sarvasya śraddhā bhavati bhārata |\nśraddhāmayo’yaṃ puruṣo yo yacchraddhaḥ sa eva saḥ ||","read":"sattvaanuroopaa sarvasya shraddhaa bhavati bhaarata |\nshraddhaamayo'yam purusho yo yachchhraddhah sa eva sah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The faith of each is shaped to his own nature, O Bhârata. The man consists of his faith; that which his faith is, he is even that.","en2":"The Shraddhâ of each is according to his natural disposition, O descendant of Bharata. The man consists of his Shraddhâ; he verily is what his Shraddhâ is.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":4,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यजन्ते सात्त्विका देवान्यक्षरक्षांसि राजसाः ।\nप्रेतान्भूतगणांश्चान्ये यजन्ते तामसा जनाः ॥","iast":"yajante sāttvikā devānyakṣarakṣāṃsi rājasāḥ |\npretānbhūtagaṇāṃścānye yajante tāmasā janāḥ ||","read":"yajante saattvikaa devaanyaksharakshaamsi raajasaah |\npretaanbhootaganaamshchaanye yajante taamasaa janaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Pure men worship the Gods; the passionate the gnomes and giants; the others, the dark folk, worship ghosts and troops of nature-spirits.","en2":"Sâttvika men worship the Devas; Râjasika, the Yakshas and the Râkshasas; the others—the Tâmasika men—the Pretas and the hosts of Bhutas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":5,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अशास्त्रविहितं घोरं तप्यन्ते ये तपो जनाः ।\nदम्भाहङ्कारसंयुक्ताः कामरागबलान्विताः ॥","iast":"aśāstravihitaṃ ghoraṃ tapyante ye tapo janāḥ |\ndambhāhaṅkārasaṃyuktāḥ kāmarāgabalānvitāḥ ||","read":"ashaastravihitam ghoram tapyante ye tapo janaah |\ndambhaahankaarasamyuktaah kaamaraagabalaanvitaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The men who perform severe austerities, unenjoined by the Scriptures, wedded to vanity and egoism, impelled by the force of their desires and passions,","en2":"Those men who practise severe austerities not enjoined by the Shâstras, given to ostentation and egoism, possessed with the power of lust and attachment, torture, senseless as they are, all the organs in the body, and Me dwelling in the body within; know them to be of Asurika resolve.","en2r":"17.5-6","rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":6,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कर्षयन्तः शरीरस्थं भूतग्राममचेतसः ।\nमां चैवान्तःशरीरस्थं तान्विद्ध्यासुरनिश्चयान् ॥","iast":"karṣayantaḥ śarīrasthaṃ bhūtagrāmamacetasaḥ |\nmāṃ caivāntaḥśarīrasthaṃ tānviddhyāsuraniścayān ||","read":"karshayantah shareerastham bhootagraamamachetasah |\nmaam chaivaantahshareerastham taanviddhyaasuranishchayaan ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Unintelligent, tormenting the aggregated elements forming the body, and Me also, seated in the inner body, know these demoniacal in their resolves.","en2":"Those men who practise severe austerities not enjoined by the Shâstras, given to ostentation and egoism, possessed with the power of lust and attachment, torture, senseless as they are, all the organs in the body, and Me dwelling in the body within; know them to be of Asurika resolve.","en2r":"17.5-6","rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":7,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आहारस्त्वपि सर्वस्य त्रिविधो भवति प्रियः ।\nयज्ञस्तपस्तथा दानं तेषां भेदमिमं शृणु ॥","iast":"āhārastvapi sarvasya trividho bhavati priyaḥ |\nyajñastapastathā dānaṃ teṣāṃ bhedamimaṃ śṛṇu ||","read":"aahaarastvapi sarvasya trividho bhavati priyah |\nyajnastapastathaa daanam teshaam bhedamimam shrinu ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The food also which is dear to each is threefold, as also sacrifice, austerity and almsgiving. Hear thou the distinction of these.","en2":"The food also which is liked by each of them is threefold, as also Yajna, austerity and almsgiving. Do thou hear this, their distinction.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":8,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"आयुःसत्त्वबलारोग्यसुखप्रीतिविवर्धनाः ।\nरस्याः स्निग्धाः स्थिरा हृद्या आहाराः सात्त्विकप्रियाः ॥","iast":"āyuḥsattvabalārogyasukhaprītivivardhanāḥ |\nrasyāḥ snigdhāḥ sthirā hṛdyā āhārāḥ sāttvikapriyāḥ ||","read":"aayuhsattvabalaarogyasukhapreetivivardhanaah |\nrasyaah snigdhaah sthiraa hridyaa aahaaraah saattvikapriyaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The foods that augment vitality, energy, vigour, health, joy and cheerfulness, delicious, bland, substantial and agreeable, are dear to the pure.","en2":"The foods which augment vitality, energy, strength, health, cheerfulness and appetite, which are savoury and oleaginous, substantial and agreeable , are liked by the Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":9,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"कट्वम्ललवणात्युष्णतीक्ष्णरूक्षविदाहिनः ।\nआहारा राजसस्येष्टा दुःखशोकामयप्रदाः ॥","iast":"kaṭvamlalavaṇātyuṣṇatīkṣṇarūkṣavidāhinaḥ |\nāhārā rājasasyeṣṭā duḥkhaśokāmayapradāḥ ||","read":"katvamlalavanaatyushnateekshnarookshavidaahinah |\naahaaraa raajasasyeshtaa duhkhashokaamayapradaah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The passionate desire foods that are bitter, sour, saline, over-hot, pungent, dry and burning and which produce pain, grief and sickness.","en2":"The foods that are bitter, sour, saline, excessively hot, pungent, dry and burning, are liked by the Râjasika, and are productive of pain, grief and disease.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":10,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यातयामं गतरसं पूति पर्युषितं च यत् ।\nउच्छिष्टमपि चामेध्यं भोजनं तामसप्रियम् ॥","iast":"yātayāmaṃ gatarasaṃ pūti paryuṣitaṃ ca yat |\nucchiṣṭamapi cāmedhyaṃ bhojanaṃ tāmasapriyam ||","read":"yaatayaamam gatarasam pooti paryushitam cha yat |\nuchchhishtamapi chaamedhyam bhojanam taamasapriyam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That which is stale and flat, putrid and corrupt, leavings also and unclean, is the food dear to the dark.","en2":"That which is stale, tasteless, stinking, cooked overnight, refuse and impure, is the food liked by the Tâmasika. [","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":11,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्यज्ञो विधिदृष्टो य इज्यते ।\nयष्टव्यमेवेति मनः समाधाय स सात्त्विकः ॥","iast":"aphalākāṅkṣibhiryajño vidhidṛṣṭo ya ijyate |\nyaṣṭavyameveti manaḥ samādhāya sa sāttvikaḥ ||","read":"aphalaakaankshibhiryajno vidhidrishto ya ijyate |\nyashtavyameveti manah samaadhaaya sa saattvikah ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The sacrifice which is offered by men without desire for fruit, as enjoined by the ordinances, under the firm belief that sacrifice is a duty, that is pure.","en2":"That Yajna is Sâttvika which is performed by men desiring no fruit, as enjoined by ordinance, with their mind fixed on the Yajna only, for its own sake.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":12,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अभिसंधाय तु फलं दम्भार्थमपि चैव यत् ।\nइज्यते भरतश्रेष्ठ तं यज्ञं विद्धि राजसम् ॥","iast":"abhisaṃdhāya tu phalaṃ dambhārthamapi caiva yat |\nijyate bharataśreṣṭha taṃ yajñaṃ viddhi rājasam ||","read":"abhisamdhaaya tu phalam dambhaarthamapi chaiva yat |\nijyate bharatashreshtha tam yajnam viddhi raajasam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The sacrifice offered with a view verily to fruit, and also indeed for self-glorification, O best of the Bhâratas; know thou that to be of passion.","en2":"That which is performed, O best of the Bhâratas, seeking for fruit and for ostentation, know it to be a Râjasika Yajna.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":13,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"विधिहीनमसृष्टान्नं मन्त्रहीनमदक्षिणम् ।\nश्रद्धाविरहितं यज्ञं तामसं परिचक्षते ॥","iast":"vidhihīnamasṛṣṭānnaṃ mantrahīnamadakṣiṇam |\nśraddhāvirahitaṃ yajñaṃ tāmasaṃ paricakṣate ||","read":"vidhiheenamasrishtaannam mantraheenamadakshinam |\nshraddhaavirahitam yajnam taamasam parichakshate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The sacrifice contrary to the ordinances, without distributing food, devoid of words of power and without gifts, empty of faith, is said to be of darkness.","en2":"The Yajna performed without heed to ordinance, in which no food is distributed, which is devoid of Mantras, gifts, and Shraddhâ, is said to be Tâmasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":14,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"देवद्विजगुरुप्राज्ञपूजनं शौचमार्जवम् ।\nब्रह्मचर्यमहिंसा च शारीरं तप उच्यते ॥","iast":"devadvijaguruprājñapūjanaṃ śaucamārjavam |\nbrahmacaryamahiṃsā ca śārīraṃ tapa ucyate ||","read":"devadvijagurupraajnapoojanam shauchamaarjavam |\nbrahmacharyamahimsaa cha shaareeram tapa uchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Worship given to the Gods, to the twice-born, to the teachers and to the wise, purity, straightforwardness, continence and harmlessness, are called the austerity of the body.","en2":"Worship of the Devas, the twice-born, the Gurus and the wise, purity, straightforwardness, continence, and non-injury are called the austerity of the body.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":15,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अनुद्वेगकरं वाक्यं सत्यं प्रियहितं च यत् ।\nस्वाध्यायाभ्यसनं चैव वाङ्मयं तप उच्यते ॥","iast":"anudvegakaraṃ vākyaṃ satyaṃ priyahitaṃ ca yat |\nsvādhyāyābhyasanaṃ caiva vāṅmayaṃ tapa ucyate ||","read":"anudvegakaram vaakyam satyam priyahitam cha yat |\nsvaadhyaayaabhyasanam chaiva vaanmayam tapa uchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Speech causing no annoyance, truthful, pleasant and beneficial, the practice of the study of the Scriptures, are called the austerity of speech.","en2":"Speech which causes no vexation, and is true, as also agreeable and beneficial, and regular study of the Vedas,— these are said to form the austerity of speech.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":16,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मनःप्रसादः सौम्यत्वं मौनमात्मविनिग्रहः ।\nभावसंशुद्धिरित्येतत्तपो मानसमुच्यते ॥","iast":"manaḥprasādaḥ saumyatvaṃ maunamātmavinigrahaḥ |\nbhāvasaṃśuddhirityetattapo mānasamucyate ||","read":"manahprasaadah saumyatvam maunamaatmavinigrahah |\nbhaavasamshuddhirityetattapo maanasamuchyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Mental happiness, equilibrium, silence, self-control, purity of nature—these are called the austerity of the mind.","en2":"Serenity of mind, kindliness, silence, self-control, honesty of motive,—this is called the mental austerity.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":17,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"श्रद्धया परया तप्तं तपस्तत्त्रिविधं नरैः ।\nअफलाकाङ्क्षिभिर्युक्तैः सात्त्विकं परिचक्षते ॥","iast":"śraddhayā parayā taptaṃ tapastattrividhaṃ naraiḥ |\naphalākāṅkṣibhiryuktaiḥ sāttvikaṃ paricakṣate ||","read":"shraddhayaa parayaa taptam tapastattrividham naraih |\naphalaakaankshibhiryuktaih saattvikam parichakshate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"This threefold austerity, performed by men with the utmost faith, without desire for fruit, harmonised, is said to be pure.","en2":"This threefold austerity practised by steadfast men, with great Shraddhâ, desiring no fruit, is said to be Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":18,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सत्कारमानपूजार्थं तपो दम्भेन चैव यत् ।\nक्रियते तदिह प्रोक्तं राजसं चलमध्रुवम् ॥","iast":"satkāramānapūjārthaṃ tapo dambhena caiva yat |\nkriyate tadiha proktaṃ rājasaṃ calamadhruvam ||","read":"satkaaramaanapoojaartham tapo dambhena chaiva yat |\nkriyate tadiha proktam raajasam chalamadhruvam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"The austerity which is practised with the object of gaining respect, honour and worship, and for ostentation, is said to be of passion, unstable and fleeting.","en2":"That austerity which is practised with the object of gaining welcome, honour and worship, and with ostentation, is here said to be Râjasika, unstable and transitory.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":19,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"मूढग्राहेणात्मनो यत्पीडया क्रियते तपः ।\nपरस्योत्सादनार्थं वा तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् ॥","iast":"mūḍhagrāheṇātmano yatpīḍayā kriyate tapaḥ |\nparasyotsādanārthaṃ vā tattāmasamudāhṛtam ||","read":"moodhagraahenaatmano yatpeedayaa kriyate tapah |\nparasyotsaadanaartham vaa tattaamasamudaahritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That austerity done under a deluded understanding, with self-torture, or with the object of destroying another, that is declared of darkness.","en2":"That austerity which is practised out of a foolish notion, with self-torture or for the purpose of wining another, is declared to be Tâmasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":20,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"दातव्यमिति यद्दानं दीयतेऽनुपकारिणे ।\nदेशे काले च पात्रे च तद्दानं सात्त्विकं स्मृतम् ॥","iast":"dātavyamiti yaddānaṃ dīyate’nupakāriṇe |\ndeśe kāle ca pātre ca taddānaṃ sāttvikaṃ smṛtam ||","read":"daatavyamiti yaddaanam deeyate'nupakaarine |\ndeshe kaale cha paatre cha taddaanam saattvikam smritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That alms given to one who does nothing in return, believing that a gift ought to be made in a fit place and time to a worthy person, that alms is accounted pure.","en2":"To give is right, gift given with this idea, to one who does no service in return, in a fit place and to a worthy person, that gift is held to be Sâttvika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":21,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यत्तु प्रत्युपकारार्थं फलमुद्दिश्य वा पुनः ।\nदीयते च परिक्लिष्टं तद्दानं राजसं स्मृतम् ॥","iast":"yattu pratyupakārārthaṃ phalamuddiśya vā punaḥ |\ndīyate ca parikliṣṭaṃ taddānaṃ rājasaṃ smṛtam ||","read":"yattu pratyupakaaraartham phalamuddishya vaa punah |\ndeeyate cha pariklishtam taddaanam raajasam smritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That given with a view to receiving in return, or looking for fruit again, or grudgingly, that alms is accounted of passion.","en2":"And what is given with a view to receiving in return, or looking for the fruit, or again reluctantly, that gift is held to be Râjasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":22,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अदेशकाले यद्दानमपात्रेभ्यश्च दीयते ।\nअसत्कृतमवज्ञातं तत्तामसमुदाहृतम् ॥","iast":"adeśakāle yaddānamapātrebhyaśca dīyate |\nasatkṛtamavajñātaṃ tattāmasamudāhṛtam ||","read":"adeshakaale yaddaanamapaatrebhyashcha deeyate |\nasatkritamavajnaatam tattaamasamudaahritam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"That alms given at unfit place and time, and to unworthy persons, disrespectfully and contemptuously, that is declared of darkness.","en2":"The gift that is given at the wrong place or time, to unworthy persons, without regard or with disdain, that is declared to be Tâmasika.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":23,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"ॐतत्सदिति निर्देशो ब्रह्मणस्त्रिविधः स्मृतः ।\nब्राह्मणास्तेन वेदाश्च यज्ञाश्च विहिताः पुरा ॥","iast":"oṃtatsaditi nirdeśo brahmaṇastrividhaḥ smṛtaḥ |\nbrāhmaṇāstena vedāśca yajñāśca vihitāḥ purā ||","read":"omtatsaditi nirdesho brahmanastrividhah smritah |\nbraahmanaastena vedaashcha yajnaashcha vihitaah puraa ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"\" Aum Tat Sat,\" this has been considered to be the threefold designation of the Eternal. By that were ordained of old Brâhmanas, Vedas and sacrifices.","en2":"\"Om, Tat, Sat\": this has been declared to be the triple designation of Brahman. By that were made of old the Brâhmanas, the Vedas and the Yajnas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":24,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तस्मादोमित्युदाहृत्य यज्ञदानतपःक्रियाः ।\nप्रवर्तन्ते विधानोक्ताः सततं ब्रह्मवादिनाम् ॥","iast":"tasmādomityudāhṛtya yajñadānatapaḥkriyāḥ |\npravartante vidhānoktāḥ satataṃ brahmavādinām ||","read":"tasmaadomityudaahritya yajnadaanatapahkriyaah |\npravartante vidhaanoktaah satatam brahmavaadinaam ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Therefore with the pronunciation of \" Aum \" the acts of sacrifice, gift and austerity as laid down in the ordinances are always commenced by the knowers of the Eternal.","en2":"Therefore, uttering 'Om,' are the acts of sacrifice, gift and austerity as enjoined in the ordinances, always begun by the followers of the Vedas.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":25,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"तदित्यनभिसन्धाय फलं यज्ञतपःक्रियाः ।\nदानक्रियाश्च विविधाः क्रियन्ते मोक्षकाङ्क्षिभिः ॥","iast":"tadityanabhisandhāya phalaṃ yajñatapaḥkriyāḥ |\ndānakriyāśca vividhāḥ kriyante mokṣakāṅkṣibhiḥ ||","read":"tadityanabhisandhaaya phalam yajnatapahkriyaah |\ndaanakriyaashcha vividhaah kriyante mokshakaankshibhih ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"With the pronunciation of \" Tat \" and without aiming at fruit are performed the various acts of sacrifice, austerity and gift, by those desiring liberation.","en2":"Uttering Tat, without aiming at fruits, are the various acts of Yajna, austerity and gift performed by the seekers of Moksha.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":26,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"सद्भावे साधुभावे च सदित्येतत्प्रयुज्यते ।\nप्रशस्ते कर्मणि तथा सच्छब्दः पार्थ युज्यते ॥","iast":"sadbhāve sādhubhāve ca sadityetatprayujyate |\npraśaste karmaṇi tathā sacchabdaḥ pārtha yujyate ||","read":"sadbhaave saadhubhaave cha sadityetatprayujyate |\nprashaste karmani tathaa sachchhabdah paartha yujyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"\" Sat \" is used in the sense of reality and goodness; likewise, O Pârtha, the word \" Sat \" is used in the sense of a good work.","en2":"The word Sat is used in the sense of reality and of goodness; and so also, Pârtha, the word Sat is used in the sense of an auspicious act.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":27,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"यज्ञे तपसि दाने च स्थितिः सदिति चोच्यते ।\nकर्म चैव तदर्थीयं सदित्येवाभिधीयते ॥","iast":"yajñe tapasi dāne ca sthitiḥ saditi cocyate |\nkarma caiva tadarthīyaṃ sadityevābhidhīyate ||","read":"yajne tapasi daane cha sthitih saditi chochyate |\nkarma chaiva tadartheeyam sadityevaabhidheeyate ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Steadfastness in sacrifice, austerity and gift is also called \" Sat \", and action for the sake of the Supreme is also named \" Sat.\"","en2":"Steadiness in Yajna, austerity and gift is also called 'Sat': as also action in connection with these (or, action for the sake of the Lord) is called Sat.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null},{"v":28,"sp":"krishna","spm":null,"spl":null,"spp":null,"sa":"अश्रद्धया हुतं दत्तं तपस्तप्तं कृतं च यत् ।\nअसदित्युच्यते पार्थ न च तत्प्रेत्य नो इह ॥","iast":"aśraddhayā hutaṃ dattaṃ tapastaptaṃ kṛtaṃ ca yat |\nasadityucyate pārtha na ca tatpretya no iha ||","read":"ashraddhayaa hutam dattam tapastaptam kritam cha yat |\nasadityuchyate paartha na cha tatpretya no iha ||","spli":null,"splr":null,"en":"Whatsoever is wrought without faith, oblation, gift, austerity, or other deed, \"Asat\" it is called, O Pârtha; it is nought, here or hereafter.","en2":"Whatever is sacrificed, given or performed, and whatever austerity is practised without Shraddhâ, it is called Asat, O Pârtha; it is naught here or hereafter.","en2r":null,"rv":null,"kid":null}];
